--- A geometric utility type representing the rectangular bounding volume. Create a new bounds by giving it a minimum and maximum range as `vec3`s

---@class bounds
---@overload fun(...): bounds
bounds = {}

--- This method has two variants, the first `bounds.intersects(other)` checks to see whether two bounds values intersect
--- 
--- The second form, `bounds.intersects(origin, dir)` returns `true` if the given ray (specified by `origin`, `dir` intersects the bounds
---@return any boolean, whether this bounding volume intersects another or the given ray
function bounds:intersects() end

--- This method has two variants, the first `bounds.intersects(other)` checks to see whether two bounds values intersect
--- 
--- The second form, `bounds.intersects(origin, dir)` returns `true` if the given ray (specified by `origin`, `dir` intersects the bounds
---@param other any bounds, another bounds value to test for intersection with
---@return any boolean, whether this bounding volume intersects another or the given ray
function bounds:intersects(other) end

--- This method has two variants, the first `bounds.intersects(other)` checks to see whether two bounds values intersect
--- 
--- The second form, `bounds.intersects(origin, dir)` returns `true` if the given ray (specified by `origin`, `dir` intersects the bounds
---@param origin any vec3, point defining the origin of the ray to test for intersection with
---@param dir any vec3, vector describing the ray to test for intersection with
---@return any boolean, whether this bounding volume intersects another or the given ray
